Given that you have a TGA framebuffer, you should be able to run X by 
starting it as root with the '-keepPriv' option.

TGAs don't need BWX, but the privilege separation code tries to 
initialize it early while X is still running as root, and before the 
configuration file has been parsed, to discover that the wsfb driver 
will be used.

-- 
Matthieu Herrb

